  "notes": "Geometric density-peak extraction on official Opus 5 GDPval-AA v2 chart. Y axis is a BROKEN linear scale: calibrated strictly on the 1200-1900 Elo region (all recovered markers fall in this range); region below 1200 down to 0 is a compressed break, not linearly continuous with the calibrated zone, and was not used. GPT-5.6 Sol series shares its light-gray marker/line color with the chart's vertical gridlines (same discrimination approach as the companion Frontier-Bench chart: density-peak blob detection with widened gray window and min_count=1200). GPT-5.6 Sol has only 4 markers on this chart (its effort ladder stops before xhigh/max) vs 5 for the other three series \u2014 assigned low/medium/high/xhigh left-to-right; 'max' not present on the chart, not fabricated. Opus 4.8 (blue) recovered via the same new 'blue' SERIES_COLORS entry as the companion chart. Elo stays raw; do not convert.",
